\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Three-pane courtroom interface for the Delhi case: Case File dossier (left), courtroom arena (center), and Transcript/Advocate Console (right). The opening judge turn is persisted and rendered in the right panel.}}{13}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Right-hand transcript panel during a live streamed witness response. The witness states nine summons and the arrest date, and expressly says the record does not state the individual dates --- the behaviour produced by the grounding prompt and the runtime grounding check of \S 4.4.}}{14}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Vector-only retrieval measured directly from \texttt {data/eval/ablation\_gold.json}: MRR@10 and top-1 accuracy for the benchmark and held-out question sets, at document level and at gold-chunk (paragraph-anchored) level.}}{17}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Case File tab for \texttt {delhi-liquor-2022}: exhibits on the left, indexed corpus chunks on the right.}}{25}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces RAG Research tab for the Delhi case. Question, retrieved chunks and source labels (BNS \S 61(2), BSA \S 63, PMLA \S 3) are shown.}}{26}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Witness Lab tab for the Delhi case. Asked for the summons count and dates, the persona replies with what the record contains --- nine summons under Section 50 PMLA between Oct 2023 and Mar 2024 --- and adds that no further specific dates are provided in the record.}}{27}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Right-panel ruling on the student's objection. The ruling distinguishes Exhibit A (the summons chronology) from the device-seizure exhibit and cites Section 63, the provision actually on record; the pre-fix version of this figure imported Section 65B of the Information Technology Act, which appears nowhere in the corpus.}}{28}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Verdict summary for the Delhi case. Scores, strengths and weaknesses for the session are shown. Bench-persona details are fictional.}}{29}{}%
